**Critic, wave 1** — continue: 9 findings stand up to the evidence, 5 questioned ('Vogel et al. (2507.18752): Shi-Fuller sterile-nu DM is viable for initial L >~ 0.5 (L give': Neither excerpt contains the claimed values. tc-35 is the title page and tc-40 is Fig. 4 text about 20 MeV asymmetry configurations. Missing: L >~ 0.5 at 10 GeV, m_s >~ 35 keV, sin^2 2theta <~ 1e-14, m_th > 8.5 keV (Zelko+) and the >>95% CL exclusion for L < 0.1. The Fig. 7 range (1e-15 to 1e-13) conflicts with the fit range in f-002 (up to 3e-13). The board brief says m_s >~ 10 keV for the same paper, which conflicts with 35 keV.; '2507.18752 provides fitting functions valid for 15 keV <= m_s <= 60 keV and 1e-15 <= sin^2': The excerpts (the same as f-001) show none of the fit coefficients, the m_th mapping, or the Villasenor 4.1 (+33.3/-1.5) keV value. Re-evaluating the stated fits at 37 keV and sin^2 2theta = 1.5e-14 gives L of about 0.68, which agrees. It gives m_th = 1.329 x 37^1.044 x (1.5e-14)^0.055, about 10.0 keV, not the claimed 8.6 keV. So either the transcribed coefficients or the hand arithmetic are wrong, and this also moves the m_s >~ 35 keV edge.; 'Model dependence: Froustey and Pitrou (2405.06509), using full 3-flavor neutrino transport': Both excerpts are title and author blocks. The quoted phrase 'generically unbound' and the reasoning that the CMB bound is at least quadratic do not appear in the evidence.; 'XRISM 2510.24560 (stacked spectra of 10 clusters, 3.75 Ms) gives a 3-sigma upper limit of ': Excerpts tc-37 (affiliations) and tc-41 (NXB modelling) do not contain the 0.95e-6 ph/cm^2/s flux limit, the Gamma < 0.97e-27 s^-1 limit, or the f1(E) polynomial. Recomputing from the stated polynomial reproduces the hand values (f1(3.55) of about 1.18 gives 4.8e-10, and 5.7e-11 at 10 keV), so the arithmetic is consistent. The source values still need a verbatim excerpt.).

Issues: The baseline numbers are internally inconsistent. Offsets of +0.48 sigma in Yp and -4.15 sigma in D/H (sigma = 0.025e-5) give chi^2 of about 17.4, not the tool's 2.77. The tool's likelihood must include an extra D/H theory error, so the '-4.1 sigma' statement misdescribes it. The negative Delta chi^2 values and the Delta N_eff exclusion threshold depend on this error budget.; The 1.5% gap from the analytic formula comes mostly from display rounding (2.5e-10 printed, 2.545e-10 used). The missing 50 keV limit is a gap in the tool, not a physical allowance. Published NuSTAR GC, INTEGRAL and Lyman-alpha limits exclude DW-DM at 50 keV, and the write-up should say so.; The DW viable region relies on the tool's tabulated X-ray limits (Roach+ 2020, Dessert+ 2020). Their numerical sin^2 2theta curves were never extracted, so 'below the X-ray limits' is not quantified. The XMM blank-sky limit itself is contested in the literature (Boyarsky et al. vs Dessert et al.), and the robustness of the conclusion to that choice was not checked..
