[usage]
[directions] d-01 [closed] Use the sterile-nu tools to compute BBN (Yp, D/H, N_eff) and; d-02 [closed] Convert the 2024-2026 X-ray decay-rate limits (XRISM 2510.24; d-03 [closed] Extract the quantitative 2024-2026 resonant-production (lept; d-04 [closed] Pin down the low-mass edge of the viable band from current s; d-05 [open] Re-extract verbatim the numbers behind the contested finding; d-06 [open] Quantify the upper (X-ray) and lower (asymmetry) edges of th; d-07 [open] Robustness check of the BBN conclusions: test whether 'BBN d
**Next steps after wave 1** — This is the last wave (13 calls, about 24 minutes, at most 3 directions), so it goes to assembling a defensible final answer rather than new exploration. I close d-04 because its goal, the structure-formation low-mass edge, is now covered by the first direction: that edge turns on the m_th > 8.5 keV bound and the disputed m_th fit (10.0 vs 8.6 keV at the benchmark). A broad new Lyman-alpha or satellite survey would not fit the budget. The first direction answers the critic's high-priority request: verbatim support for the contested findings f-001, f-002, f-004, f-009 and f-011, mostly read from full texts already downloaded, which keeps the call count low. The second is the core deliverable and the cross-check against the literature: it digitizes the published X-ray and asymmetry edges at 15-60 keV and checks them against a single tool grid call, giving a viable-interval table per asymmetry scenario. The third, lowest priority, is a robustness check of the BBN conclusion under other likelihood error budgets, plus a quantitative estimate of the lepton-asymmetry effect on Yp, which the tool does not model. The task does not ask for facility runs, so none is scheduled. Planned use is about 10 tool calls.

New lines of investigation: Re-extract verbatim the numbers behind the contested findings f-001, f-002, f-004 and f-009. Resolve the m_th fit inconsistency so the low-mass edge of the resonant window is set consistently, absorbing the structure-formation edge goal of d-04.; Quantify the upper (X-ray) and lower (asymmetry) edges of the viable band at 15, 20, 30, 40 and 60 keV, and assemble one viable-region table per asymmetry scenario.; Robustness check of the BBN conclusions: test whether 'BBN does not bind keV sterile-neutrino DM' survives other error budgets, and estimate the Yp shift from lepton asymmetry that the tool omits..
[wave 1] end d-01, d-02, d-03 -> continue
