**Finding:** In the sterile-nu tool, the X-ray exclusion boundary at m_s = 20 keV lies between sin^2 2theta = 1e-13 (not excluded, Gamma = 4.36e-29 s^-1) and 1e-12 (excluded by NuSTAR M31, d-02). At 30 keV the tool flags nothing even at sin^2 2theta = 1e-11 (Gamma = 3.31e-26 s^-1, E = 15 keV). The tool therefore has no tabulated X-ray limit for line energies above about 10-13 keV (m_s >~ 25 keV), which explains why it cannot reproduce the NuSTAR-GC / INTEGRAL upper edge at 30-60 keV.
