**Finding:** The m_th fit in 2507.18752 Eq. 8 has verbatim coefficients A = 1.329, a = 1.044, b = 0.055 (keV units), so at the paper's own benchmark (m_s = 37 keV, sin^2 2theta = 1.5e-14) m_th = 1.329 x 37^1.044 x (1.5e-14)^0.055 = 10.0 keV, not 8.6 keV. The f-002 value of 8.6 keV is an arithmetic error. The L fit (Eq. 9: C = 1.865e-12, alpha = -1.813, beta = -1.042) gives L = 0.68 at the same point, which confirms that part of f-002.
