[finding] f-019 The consistent low-mass edge from m_th > 8.5 keV (Zelko+, 95% CL) uses the verified 2507.18752 Eq. 8: m_s,min = [8.5/(1.329 (sin^2 2theta)^0.055)]^(1/1.044) keV
**Finding:** The consistent low-mass edge from m_th > 8.5 keV (Zelko+, 95% CL) uses the verified 2507.18752 Eq. 8: m_s,min = [8.5/(1.329 (sin^2 2theta)^0.055)]^(1/1.044) keV. By hand this gives m_s,min of about 36.5 keV at sin^2 2theta = 1e-15, 32.3 keV at 1e-14, 31.6 keV at 1.5e-14 and 28.6 keV at 1e-13. The L = 0.5 contour (Eq. 9) crosses the m_th = 8.5 keV line near m_s of about 31 keV and sin^2 2theta of about 2.8e-14. At sin^2 2theta = 1e-14 the edge point needs L of about 1.35. The paper's rounded summary 'm_s >~ 35 keV, sin^2 2theta <~ 1e-14, L >~ 0.5' (verbatim, Sec. IV) is consistent with this to within the fit and figure-reading precision; the X-ray exclusion, which I did not check, presumably cuts the larger-mixing corner. The board brief's 'm_s >~ 10 keV' is wrong and should read m_s >~ 30-37 keV (paper: >~ 35 keV).
