**Finding:** I verified the f-001/f-002 items in 2507.18752 verbatim. The fit validity range is '15 keV≤m s≤60 keV and 10^−15≤sin2(2θ)≤3×10^−13'; average errors are 1.3% (m_th) and 8.3% (L). Further quotes: 'excluded at much greater than 95% CL forL<0.1'; 'mth = 4.1+33.3 −1.5 keV [20]'; 'mth >8.4 keV (95% CL) [18] andm th >8.5 keV (95% CL) [19]'; Eq. 7 'mth,new≈0.83m th,old + 0.36'; Fig. 7 caption: initial L 'given atT= 10 GeV' and 'reduced by a factor of 5 to 10 byT= 10 MeV'. Fig. 7 has m_s axis ticks 15-60 keV and sin^2 2theta tick labels 1e-15, 1e-14 and 1e-13. This does not contradict the fit-validity upper end of 3e-13: the figure's labelled ticks and the fit's validation range are different quantities.
