[direction] d-06 -> blocked (The published limit curves (1609.00667 Figs. 7-8, 2507.20659 Fig. 1) cannot be extracted from HTML, and the tool has no X-ray limits above m_s of about 25 keV, so I could not quantify the upper and lower edges at 30-60 keV.)
**Blocked — Quantify the upper (X-ray) and lower (asymmetry) edges of the viable band at 15, 20, 30, 40 and 60 keV, and assemble one viable-region table per asymmetry scenario..** (The published limit curves (1609.00667 Figs. 7-8, 2507.20659 Fig. 1) cannot be extracted from HTML, and the tool has no X-ray limits above m_s of about 25 keV, so I could not quantify the upper and lower edges at 30-60 keV.) I could not build the viable-region table, because the published X-ray edges and the zero-asymmetry lower edges are only available as plots I could not extract. What the tools did give is below.

1) Tool grid (DW production; m_s = 15, 20, 30, 40, 60 keV; sin^2 2theta from 1e-15 to 1e-11; 45 points; file /Users/nramachandra/hep-genesis-testing/projects/ramp-combo-sterile-bbn-xray/runs/261021_143100/sterile_nu_grid_DW_677e35.csv):
- BBN excludes nothing. |Delta chi^2| is at most 0.0044 and Delta N_eff at most 3.4e-4 (f-015).
- Only the point at 60 keV, sin^2 2theta = 1e-11 overcloses under DW (Omega h^2 = 0.22).
- The grid output has no X-ray flag column, so I ran the separate X-ray tool at selected points.

2) Tool X-ray flags:
- 15 keV, sin^2 2theta = 1e-12: excluded by NuSTAR M31 and XMM blank sky (Gamma = 1.03e-28 s^-1).
- 20 keV: the tool's exclusion boundary lies between 1e-13 (not excluded, Gamma = 4.36e-29 s^-1) and 1e-12 (excluded, from d-02).
- 30 keV at 1e-13 and 1e-11, 40 keV at 1e-14, and 60 keV at 1e-14: none are flagged. At 30 keV, 1e-11 the rate is Gamma = 3.31e-26 s^-1.
- So the tool has no tabulated X-ray limits for line energies above about 10-13 keV (m_s above about 25 keV) (f-016, f-017).
- The mismatch with the published limits comes from these missing limits, not from the decay-rate normalization, which matches 1.38e-32 (sin^2 2theta/1e-10)(m/keV)^5.

3) Figure extraction failed for both papers (dead end x-02). 1609.00667 exposes only Figs. 3-4 in its HTML version, and 2507.20659 has no extractable figures. I have no digitized NuSTAR or INTEGRAL edge and no zero-asymmetry lower edge.

What this leaves:
- The success criteria are not met: I have no viable interval at five or more masses and no agreement within a factor of 2 with digitized curves, because no curves were digitized.
- Partial edges from the board: at 15 keV the upper edge is below 1e-12 (tool). The scenario with L around 0.5-1 is viable only at m_s of about 35 keV or more and sin^2 2theta of about 1e-14 or less (f-001). The flavor-universal case with L around 1e-3 is excluded across 15-60 keV for full-DM production, since 2507.18752 excludes the window at L < 0.1.
- I did not address the Dessert vs Boyarsky blank-sky controversy beyond noting that the tool uses Dessert+2020.

